- # Soundness Benchmarking Standards
+ # Standard di benchmarking di Soundness

- This document defines how benchmarks are written and organised in the Soundness
- libraries. Benchmarks build on [Probably](https://github.com/propensive/probably/)
- and, for staged compiletime work, on [Sedentary](https://github.com/propensive/sedentary/).
- It complements `testing.md`. Examples are drawn from `lib/*/src/bench/*.scala`.
+ Questo documento definisce come si scrivono e si organizzano i benchmark nelle librerie Soundness.
+ I benchmark si basano su [Probably](https://github.com/propensive/probably/) e, per il lavoro in
+ staging a tempo di compilazione, su [Sedentary](https://github.com/propensive/sedentary/). Integra
+ `testing.md`. Gli esempi sono tratti da `lib/*/src/bench/*.scala`.

- ## 1. Location and naming
+ ## 1. Posizione e nomi

- Benchmarks live in a module's `src/bench` directory, in a file named
- `<module>.Benchmarks.scala`. The object extends `Suite` and is conventionally
- named `Benchmarks`:
+ I benchmark si trovano nella directory `src/bench` di un modulo, in un file chiamato
+ `<module>.Benchmarks.scala`. L'oggetto estende `Suite` e per convenzione si chiama `Benchmarks`:

= named `Benchmarks`:
=
